bic_trace_step.reason:
The function `rxgk_verify_response()` contains the inverted conditional check on the authenticator length. Specifically, in lines 968-970:

	auth_len	= ntohl(xauth_len);
	if (auth_len < len)
		goto short_packet;

This check incorrectly rejects packets where the authenticator length (`auth_len`) is less than the remaining packet length (`len`), and allows packets where `auth_len` is greater than `len` (oversized) to proceed, which eventually triggers a kernel panic in `__skb_to_sgvec()` during decryption.
